      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: C Partial isolation results in vacant staring, self-mutilation, and stereotyped behavior. Total isolation leads to self-orality, self-clasping, and fearful behaviors among peers. Nonhuman primates reared only by their mother results in failure to leave mother and explore. These primates may be terrified when exposed to peers.",
